    "flow": [
      { "text": "este, ese, aquel…", "variant": "prep" },
      { "text": "noun", "variant": "verb" },
      { "text": "aquí · ahí · allí" }
    ],
    "qa": [
      {
        "html": "<strong>este</strong> = near me (<em>aquí</em>). <strong>ese</strong> = near you, or not far (<em>ahí</em>). <strong>aquel</strong> = far from us both (<em>allí</em>).",
        "tag": "Near or far"
      },
      {
        "html": "They match the noun: <em>este piso, esta casa, estos pisos, estas casas</em>. Careful with the masculine: <em>aquel</em> has no <em>-e</em>, and it is not <em>aquello</em>.",
        "tag": "Four forms"
      },
      {
        "html": "They can stand alone: <em>¿Quieres esta camisa o esa?</em> The RAE does not ask for an accent here. Write <em>este, esa</em>.",
        "tag": "Without a noun"
      },
      {
        "html": "<strong>esto, eso, aquello</strong> are for something you do not name or do not know yet. They do not change and never go before a noun: <em>¿Qué es esto? No entiendo eso.</em>",
        "tag": "esto, eso"
      },
      {
        "html": "To say which one, ask with <strong>¿cuál?</strong> (plural <em>¿cuáles?</em>): <em>¿Cuál quieres? – Este.</em> <strong>esta</strong> (this) has no accent, but <strong>está</strong> (is) does: <em>Esta casa está aquí.</em>",
        "tag": "¿cuál?"
      }
    ],
    "noteHtml": "Common mistakes: ✗ <em>esto libro</em> → ✓ <em>este libro</em>. ✗ <em>este casa</em> → ✓ <em>esta casa</em>. ✗ <em>aquello coche</em> → ✓ <em>aquel coche</em>. ✗ <em>esta aquí</em> for “is here” → ✓ <em>está aquí</em>.",
    "reference": {
      "showLabel": "Show overview ▼",
      "hideLabel": "Hide overview ▲",
